{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויקהל", :translit "vayakhel", :gloss "and he assembled"} {:he "כי קרן עור פניו", :translit "ki karan or panav", :gloss "for the skin of his face shone"} {:he "פ' שבת", :translit "parashat shabbat", :gloss "the portion of Shabbat"} {:he "ואמר ויקהל", :translit "ve'amar vayakhel", :gloss "and he said 'and he assembled'"} {:he "פ' שבת", :translit "parashat shabbat", :gloss "the portion of Shabbat"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut of parashiyot: the verse about Moses' radiant face (Exodus 34:29-35) is adjacent to the Shabbat portion (Exodus 35:1-3), teaching that Shabbat radiance differs from weekday radiance."}], :frame {:text "Exodus 34:29-35 describes Moses' face radiating light after descending from Sinai. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition of that narrative to the Shabbat command at Exodus 35:1 as itself a teaching about Shabbat. The word ויקהל ('and he assembled') further hints that on Shabbatot and festivals the people gather to hear derashot, as the verse describes Moses commanding the assembled congregation.", :sources ["Exodus 34:29" "Exodus 35:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לעשות", :translit "la'asot", :gloss "to do"} {:he "אשר ברא אלהים לעשות", :translit "asher bara elohim la'asot", :gloss "which Elohim created to do"} {:he "ויכולו", :translit "vayekhulu", :gloss "and they were finished"} {:he "מויקהל עד לא תבערו וגו' ביום השבת", :translit "mivayakhel ad lo teva'aru etc. beyom hashabbat", :gloss "from 'and he assembled' until 'you shall not kindle etc. on the day of Shabbat'"} {:he "לא תבערו", :translit "lo teva'aru", :gloss "you shall not kindle"} {:he "השבת", :translit "hashabbat", :gloss "the Shabbat"} {:he "לא תבערו", :translit "lo teva'aru", :gloss "you shall not kindle"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ל״ תׁ", :b "תשע"} {:kind :other, :note "לעשות is written defective (without vav); combined with ל״ and תׁ = 9, hinting to 39 melakhot done in 6 days, not on Shabbat."} {:kind :masorah, :count 39, :occurrences ["תיבות"]} {:kind :other, :note "From ויקהל until לא תבערו ביום השבת there are 39 words, excluding the word השבת."} {:kind :other, :note "The word לא תבערו is singled out because fire was needed for Mishkan construction: cooking spices, dyeing, and refining metals."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah at Shabbat 7:2 enumerates 39 avot melakhah (primary categories of labor), corresponding to the labors required for constructing the Mishkan. Tractate Shabbat 49b derives that the 39 melakhot are learned from the juxtaposition of the Mishkan construction (Exodus 35–39) to the Shabbat prohibition (Exodus 35:2-3). The prohibition against kindling fire on Shabbat is stated separately at Exodus 35:3; Rashbam on Exodus 35:3 explains this emphasis because fire was essential for the Mishkan's dyes and metalwork. The phrase 'asher bara elohim la'asot' appears at Genesis 2:3, concluding the creation account.", :sources ["Shabbat 7:2" "Shabbat 49b" "Exodus 35:2" "Exodus 35:3" "Genesis 2:3" "Rashbam Exodus 35:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut of parashiyot: the verse about Moses' radiant face (Exodus 34:29-35) is adjacent to the Shabbat portion (Exodus 35:1-3), teaching that Shabbat radiance differs from weekday radiance.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ל״ תׁ", :a-value 430, :b "תשע", :b-value 770, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "לעשות is written defective (without vav); combined with ל״ and תׁ = 9, hinting to 39 melakhot done in 6 days, not on Shabbat.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 39, :occurrences ["תיבות"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "תיבות", :refs ["Genesis 6:14" "Exodus 2:3"], :n 2, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "From ויקהל until לא תבערו ביום השבת there are 39 words, excluding the word השבת.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "The word לא תבערו is singled out because fire was needed for Mishkan construction: cooking spices, dyeing, and refining metals.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:08.588080464Z", :model "glm-5.2"}